Z||000017||Hock||06-01-99||12:10 PM||||Hooker Headers are still avaliable for the four cyc. here is the information:<br>      Emission legal-#4703 $275.00<br>      Off Road Version (eliminates converter)-#4702 $260.00<p>That is the only header I have been able to find for my fiero so there it is.
Z||000018||Racer 1||06-02-99||11:06 AM||||Hey YO, I have a HOOKER super competion header on my fiero.theres two types a 4 into 2 into 1  or 4 into one.The 4 into 1 doesent have a sensor mount on it for emissions..I got mine 4-2-1 header from summit racing for around 227.00$$ then wrapped it with header wrap to keep stuff COOOOL.Its a heel-a-lot better then the wimpy stock manifold!I also took out my muffler and just runned two 4" monza tips out back! this gave me alot more HP !!!!!!!!    GOOD LUCK
Z||000019||Scott2M4||01-12-2000||07:39 AM||||Please pardon my ignorance ...<P>Do these headers directly replace the stock 4 cylinder exhaust manifold - without any modifications?  Is it a waste of money to purchase them if they'll be running with an otherwise stock exhaust system?  Also, Racer 1 mentioned that the 4-&gt;1 system doesn't have an O2 sensor mount.  Does the 4-&gt;2-&gt;1 system have it?<P>Does Hooker have a website?<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000020||2FAST4U||01-11-2000||11:44 PM||||You will need a slip on reducer to hook up the Hooker header to your stock exhaust.<BR>The 4-2-1 header does have a fitting for the O2 sensor.<BR>While the Header will make more power with the stock exhaust, why not spend a little extra and add a better exhaust system. It's money well spent.||||reg||1
Z||000021||2FAST4U||01-12-2000||01:27 AM||||If you guys are really into building your own headers, Sanderson has some great printed material and videos on designing and building your own.<BR>I sent my head to Competition Cylinder Heads to have it pocket ported, polished, and blueprinted. While they had the head I had them weld a devider into the center exhaust port. Although I do not have the cylinder head mounted yet to test it, welding a center devider in is supposidly good for a 10% or more increase in torque.||||reg||1
